Upstream-Name: speech-dispatcher-modules
Upstream-Contact: Grigory Tuboltsev <gtubolcev@gmail.com>
Source: https://github.com/gtubolcev/linux-tts

Files: *
Copyright: 2026 Grigory Tuboltsev
License: GPL-3+

Files: vosk/vosk.c
Copyright: 2026 Grigory Tuboltsev
License: GPL-3+
Comment: A C port of the Python vosk_tts package of Alpha Cephei
 (Apache-2.0).

Files: kokoro/*
Copyright: 2026 Grigory Tuboltsev
License: GPL-3+
Comment: ru-g2p.c is a port of ru_g2p.py of zaakirio/kokoro-ru (Apache-2.0),
 of misaki's espeak front end (Apache-2.0) and of the punctuation handling of
 phonemizer (GPL-3+); en-g2p.c is a port of misaki's English G2P (en.py,
 Apache-2.0); en-tagger.c reimplements the inference of spaCy's tok2vec and
 tagger (MIT) and of its tokenizer.

Files: kokoro/misaki/*
Copyright: hexgrad and the misaki contributors
License: Apache-2.0
Comment: us_gold, us_silver, gb_gold and gb_silver .json of hexgrad/misaki
 fba1236, converted by kokoro/misaki-lexicon.py.  misaki does not say where
 the pronunciations come from (its issues 107 and 113 ask); the files carry
 no other terms than the repository's Apache-2.0.

Files: kokoro/misaki/en-tagger*
Copyright: 2021 ExplosionAI GmbH
           2016-2024 ExplosionAI GmbH, 2016 spaCy GmbH, 2015 Matthew Honnibal
License: Expat
Comment: The tok2vec and tagger weights of spaCy's en_core_web_sm 3.8.0, its
 tokenizer rules and regexes and spaCy's symbol ids (spaCy 3.8, MIT), and the
 lexeme_norm table of spacy-lookups-data 1.0.5 (MIT), exported by
 kokoro/en-tagger-export.py.  Explosion trained the model on OntoNotes 5
 (licensed by Explosion from the LDC) and publishes the weights under MIT;
 no training data is included.

Files: kokoro/espeak-ru/*
Copyright: espeak-ng contributors
License: GPL-3+
Comment: ru_rules, ru_list and ru_emoji of espeak-ng master (688cb60),
 which honour the stress mark U+0301; compiled into ru_dict at build time.

Files: teratts/teratts.c
Copyright: 2026 Grigory Tuboltsev
License: GPL-3+
Comment: Follows teratts.py of TeraSpace/TeraTTSv2 (the text preparation
 and the order of its four ONNX graphs).

Files: speechd-module/*
Copyright: 2020-2025 Samuel Thibault <samuel.thibault@ens-lyon.org>
License: BSD-2-Clause
Comment: The module library of speech-dispatcher 0.12.1, built only where
 speech-dispatcher does not install it (before 0.12.0).

